---
status: 'published';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<!-- Concept Site Banner -->
<section class="bg-indigo-50 border-b border-indigo-200">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 py-2 text-center">
    <p class="text-sm text-indigo-900">
      Concept demonstration by ImagineThis.Site: exploring what an event website
      can do.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
<Layout
  title="Human & AI Systems Summit"
  description="A one-day gathering for people designing the future of work with AI, human judgment, and better coordination."
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section
    class="relative overflow-hidden bg-gradient-to-b from-gray-50 to-white dark:from-gray-950 dark:to-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200/70 dark:border-gray-800/70"
  >
    <div
      class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-20 md:py-28 grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-10 items-center"
    >
      <!-- Copy -->
      <div class="md:col-span-6">
        <p
          class="text-sm uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 mb-4"
        >
          Concept Demonstration
        </p>
        <h1
          class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-serif font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white leading-tight"
        >
          Human & AI Systems Summit
        </h1>
        <p
          class="mt-6 text-lg md:text-xl text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed"
        >
          A one-day gathering for people designing the future of work with AI,
          human judgment, and better coordination.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-6 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
          <p>
            <span class="font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200"
              >Date:</span
            > October 24, 2026
          </p>
          <p>
            <span class="font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200"
              >Location:</span
            > Northbridge Innovation Pavilion — Riverfront District
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
          <a
            href="#apply"
            class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md bg-gray-900 dark:bg-white px-6 py-3 text-white dark:text-gray-900 font-semibold shadow-sm hover:bg-gray-800 dark:hover:bg-gray-100 transition"
          >
            Apply to Attend
          </a>
          <a
            href="#schedule"
            class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md border border-gray-300 dark:border-gray-700 px-6 py-3 text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-200 font-semibold hover:bg-gray-50 dark:hover:bg-gray-800 transition"
          >
            View Schedule
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Hero photo collage -->
      <div class="md:col-span-6">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4">
          <img
            src="/images/summit/man-listening.webp"
            alt="Attendee listening closely during a session"
            class="h-60 md:h-72 w-full object-cover rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800"
          />
          <img
            src="/images/summit/people-talking-ai-summit.webp"
            alt="Small group in conversation between sessions"
            class="h-60 md:h-72 w-full object-cover rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 mt-6 md:mt-12"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What This Demonstrates -->
  <section class="py-16 bg-white dark:bg-gray-950">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div
        class="rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 bg-stone-50 dark:bg-gray-900 p-8"
      >
        <p
          class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-orange-600 dark:text-orange-400 mb-4"
        >
          What This Demonstrates
        </p>

        <h2
          class="text-3xl font-serif font-bold text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-200 mb-6"
        >
          A website can become part of the event.
        </h2>

        <p
          class="text-lg text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mb-6 leading-relaxed"
        >
          This concept was created by ImagineThis.Site to demonstrate how an
          event website can do more than share information.
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-6">
          <div class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            • Attract the right attendees
          </div>
          <div class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            • Present speakers and programming
          </div>
          <div class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            • Communicate value clearly
          </div>
          <div class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            • Support registration and ticketing
          </div>
          <div class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            • Build anticipation before the event
          </div>
          <div class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            • Coordinate sponsors and partners
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="text-lg font-medium text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-200">
          The event is fictional. The capabilities are real.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- About -->
  <section id="about" class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-white dark:bg-gray-900">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-10">
      <div class="md:col-span-5">
        <h2
          class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white"
        >
          Why This Gathering
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div
        class="md:col-span-7 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed"
      >
        <p class="mb-5">
          AI is reshaping how teams coordinate, decide, and deliver. The Summit
          brings together designers, operators, technologists, civic leaders,
          and educators to pair human judgment with AI—so organizations get
          clearer, faster, and more capable.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5">
          Expect focused sessions, useful frameworks, and time to compare notes
          with peers doing real work in complex environments.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
          <li>Case studies and patterns you can reuse</li>
          <li>Cross‑disciplinary insight that translates to action</li>
          <li>Design‑forward environment with room to think</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Themes -->
  <section
    id="themes"
    class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-stone-50 dark:bg-gray-950 border-y border-stone-200/70 dark:border-gray-800"
  >
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <h2
          class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-6"
        >
          Themes
        </h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
          Practical patterns for making AI legible and useful across
          organizations and public spaces.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 grid md:grid-cols-3 sm:grid-cols-2 grid-cols-1 gap-6">
        {
          [
            {
              title: 'AI & Human Judgment',
              desc: 'Improve decisions while keeping accountability and context.',
            },
            {
              title: 'Future of Work',
              desc: 'Roles, workflows, and clarity in hybrid human–AI teams.',
            },
            {
              title: 'Cities & Civic Systems',
              desc: 'Public services and digital infrastructure that scale.',
            },
            {
              title: 'Organizational Coordination',
              desc: 'Visibility, responsibility, and executive sensemaking.',
            },
            {
              title: 'Digital Public Space',
              desc: 'Healthier information environments for participation.',
            },
            {
              title: 'Design for Participation',
              desc: 'Interfaces and rituals that invite real contribution.',
            },
          ].map((item) => (
            <div class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 p-6 hover:border-gray-300 dark:hover:border-gray-700 transition">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
                {item.title}
              </h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                {item.desc}
              </p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Program Highlights -->
  <section id="sessions" class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-white dark:bg-gray-900">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <h2
          class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-6"
        >
          Program Highlights
        </h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
          A focused day of keynotes, panels, and hands‑on work—built for
          operators and decision‑makers.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <div
          class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 p-6"
        >
          <p
            class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 mb-2"
          >
            Keynote
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
            Operational AI: Designing for Judgment
          </h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 text-sm">
            How to align AI tooling with roles, accountability, and service
            quality across a real organization.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 text-xs">
            Speaker: Dr. Maya Corcoran — Director, UrbanLab AI, Northbridge
            University
          </p>
        </div>

        <div
          class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 p-6"
        >
          <p
            class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 mb-2"
          >
            Panel
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
            Cities, Data, and Civic Capacity
          </h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 text-sm">
            Permitting, planning, and public communication with AI in the loop.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 text-xs">
            With: Elena Duarte (CIO, City of Graymont), Samir Koh (Exec.
            Director, Civic Tech Network), Prof. Lina Havel (Chair, Urban
            Systems, Northbridge University)
          </p>
        </div>

        <div
          class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 p-6"
        >
          <p
            class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 mb-2"
          >
            Workshop
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
            Mapping Coordination: From Roles to Interfaces
          </h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 text-sm">
            Create service maps that pair responsibilities with AI support, then
            test them against real scenarios.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 text-xs">
            Facilitator: Jordan Rivera — Principal, Studio for Civic Systems
          </p>
        </div>

        <div
          class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 p-6"
        >
          <p
            class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 mb-2"
          >
            Case Study
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
            Designing a Digital Public Space for Deliberation
          </h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 text-sm">
            A credible example of community input tools that encourage
            high‑quality contributions.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 text-xs">
            Presenter: Leah Chen — Product Lead, ForumWorks
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Schedule Timeline -->
  <section
    id="schedule"
    class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-stone-50 dark:bg-gray-950 border-y border-stone-200/70 dark:border-gray-800"
  >
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <h2
          class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-6"
        >
          Schedule (One Day)
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 relative">
        <ol
          class="relative border-l border-gray-300 dark:border-gray-700 ml-4 space-y-8"
        >
          {
            [
              {
                time: '08:30',
                title: 'Arrival & Coffee',
                desc: 'Check‑in, light breakfast, informal introductions.',
              },
              {
                time: '09:15',
                title: 'Opening Keynote',
                desc: 'Operational AI and human judgment.',
              },
              {
                time: '10:15',
                title: 'Facilitated Sessions',
                desc: 'Breakouts on work, cities, and digital public space.',
              },
              {
                time: '12:00',
                title: 'Lunch',
                desc: 'Catered lunch on site; time for hallway conversations.',
              },
              {
                time: '13:15',
                title: 'Workshops',
                desc: 'Hands‑on: mapping coordination, prototyping interfaces.',
              },
              {
                time: '15:30',
                title: 'Closing Conversation',
                desc: 'Synthesis: what to ship in the next 90 days.',
              },
              {
                time: '17:30',
                title: 'Optional Partner Dinner',
                desc: 'Hosted dinner for sponsors and professional pass holders.',
              },
            ].map((item) => (
              <li class="ml-4">
                <span class="absolute -left-1.5 mt-1.5 h-3 w-3 rounded-full bg-gray-900 dark:bg-white ring-4 ring-stone-50 dark:ring-gray-950" />
                <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-start sm:justify-between gap-2">
                  <time class="text-xs font-semibold text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
                    {item.time}
                  </time>
                  <div class="sm:w-3/4">
                    <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
                      {item.title}
                    </h3>
                    <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
                      {item.desc}
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Tickets / Passes -->
  <section id="tickets" class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-white dark:bg-gray-900">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <h2
          class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-6"
        >
          Tickets & Passes
        </h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
          Pricing reflects a focused, high‑signal gathering with practical
          outcomes.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <!-- General Pass -->
        <div
          class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 p-6 flex flex-col"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
            General Pass
          </h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
            Access to all core sessions.
          </p>
          <p
            class="mt-4 text-3xl font-serif font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white"
          >
            $95
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            <li>• Main stage + panels</li>
            <li>• One workshop</li>
            <li>• Light breakfast & lunch</li>
          </ul>
          <a
            id="apply"
            href="#apply"
            class="mt-6 inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md border border-gray-300 dark:border-gray-700 px-4 py-2 font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-200 hover:bg-gray-50 dark:hover:bg-gray-800 transition"
          >
            Reserve Your Seat
          </a>
        </div>

        <!-- Professional Pass -->
        <div
          class="rounded-xl border-2 border-gray-900 dark:border-white bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 p-6 shadow-sm flex flex-col"
        >
          <div
            class="inline-block text-xs uppercase tracking-wider bg-gray-900 dark:bg-white text-white dark:text-gray-900 px-2 py-1 rounded mb-3"
          >
            Recommended
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
            Professional Pass
          </h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
            Deeper engagement for operators and team leads.
          </p>
          <p
            class="mt-4 text-3xl font-serif font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white"
          >
            $240
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            <li>• All General benefits</li>
            <li>• Two workshops (priority)</li>
            <li>• Post‑event notes & playbooks</li>
            <li>• Professional networking circle</li>
          </ul>
          <a
            href="#apply"
            class="mt-6 inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md bg-gray-900 dark:bg-white px-4 py-2 font-semibold text-white dark:text-gray-900 hover:bg-gray-800 dark:hover:bg-gray-100 transition"
          >
            Apply to Attend
          </a>
        </div>

        <!-- Partner Dinner -->
        <div
          class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 p-6 flex flex-col"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
            Partner Dinner
          </h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
            Optional hosted dinner with speakers & sponsors.
          </p>
          <p
            class="mt-4 text-3xl font-serif font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white"
          >
            $500
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            <li>• Limited seating</li>
            <li>• Hosted by Innovation Lab & partners</li>
            <li>• Reserved table placement</li>
          </ul>
          <a
            href="#apply"
            class="mt-6 inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md border border-gray-300 dark:border-gray-700 px-4 py-2 font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-200 hover:bg-gray-50 dark:hover:bg-gray-800 transition"
          >
            Request Dinner Invite
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Venue / Atmosphere -->
  <section id="venue" class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-white dark:bg-gray-900">
    <div
      class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-10 items-center"
    >
      <div class="md:col-span-5">
        <h2
          class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white"
        >
          Venue & Atmosphere
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
          Northbridge Innovation Pavilion — a light‑filled timber‑and‑glass
          atrium in the Riverfront District. Sessions run in the Main Hall;
          workshops in Studio B; the partner dinner in the Garden Room.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="md:col-span-7">
        <div
          class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800"
        >
          <img
            src="/images/summit/atrium-human-ai-summit.webp"
            alt="Modern architectural atrium hosting a professional gathering"
            class="w-full h-[320px] md:h-[420px] object-cover"
          />
          <div
            class="absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none bg-gradient-to-t from-white/25 to-transparent dark:from-gray-900/30"
          >
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Final CTA -->
  <section class="py-20 bg-stone-50 dark:bg-gray-900">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
      <p
        class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-orange-600 dark:text-orange-400 mb-4"
      >
        Imagine This
      </p>

      <h2
        class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-serif font-bold text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-200 mb-6"
      >
        What Could Your Event Website Do?
      </h2>

      <p class="text-xl text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-8">
        This concept demonstrates how a website can help an event attract
        attendees, communicate value, and create a better experience before the
        doors even open.
      </p>

      <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-10">
        Whether you're organizing a conference, summit, workshop, retreat,
        festival, or community gathering, your website can become an active part
        of the event itself.
      </p>

      <a
        href="/contact/"
        class="inline-block bg-orange-600 text-white px-8 py-4 rounded-lg font-semibold hover:bg-orange-700 transition dark:bg-orange-500 dark:hover:bg-orange-400"
      >
        Start a Conversation
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
